{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793548208,"nonce":"Ftdp2LMVblxaWMWbwySJnCwinig=","title":"Components take Signal values and bind their props in place","message":"Every component, core (blinc_layout::widgets) and cn, approaches reactivity through Signal, Computed and Effect, and takes props by binding.\n\nValue: the entry point takes `Signal\u003cT\u003e` by value (it is Copy), not `\u0026State\u003cT\u003e`. A range is `Signal\u003cRangeInclusive\u003cf64\u003e\u003e`.\n\nProps: anything that can change at run time (disabled, label text, a value shown) takes `impl IntoReactive\u003cT\u003e` and is bound in place: an attribute through attr_when, a class through class_when, text through Text::bound, a property through the binding channel. Handlers read the bound value when the event arrives. No build-time bool captured into a closure, no Stateful rebuild to follow a prop. Structural config (size, bounds, step, options) stays plain, as in ashui.\n\nLook follows the attribute: colours that change with a prop are CSS rules keyed on the attribute, not theme colours picked at build time.\n\nShared piece: `blinc_layout::binding::Reactive\u003cT\u003e` is Clone and has `now()`, so a widget keeps one bound prop, hands clones to attr_when and reads it in handlers.\n\nEntry points taking `\u0026State\u003cT\u003e` today:\ncore: checkbox, toggle, radio_group, number_input, input_otp\ncn: checkbox, switch, toggle, toggle_group, radio_group, select, combobox, number_input, slider (NumberValue), input_otp, tabs, collapsible, sidebar, pagination\n\nEach component lands with its call sites: blinc_cn_dsl, examples, recorder and unit tests, book page and CHANGELOG. This is a break of the public API; it goes in the 0.6.0 notes (3f77b11).\n\nEarlier pass: 96b7192 moved DSL-exposed props to Reactive\u003cT\u003e but bound structural props through Stateful deps (a subtree rebuild). This replaces that mechanism.","files":null}]}